+### 9.6 Host-adapter attribution return (not a wire frame)
+
+Protocol3 (Rust major 3) and typescript-semantic (major 2) frames stay the closed
+set of §9.2 / §9.4. No `TargetAttribution` frame is added. Occupancy mapping is
+not a compiler-worker product; it is the second output of the **language
+wrapper** that already translates compiler-native resolution into opaque
+`SubjectIdV1` payload fields.
+
+Typed return envelope: `foundation/provider-target-attribution-return.schema.v2.json`
+`ProviderTargetAttributionReturnV2` `{schemaVersion:2, planId, producerClosure,
+stageOrdinal, records:[TargetAttributionV2…]}`. Adapter-stage only: not a digest
+domain, not a Run preimage, not an execution-plan `outputDomain`. Captured
+admitted V2 records remain `domain=target-attribution`.
+
+**Invocation.** After this producer's Analyze-stage fact2 identities are minted
+from the worker FactBatch, and before `attach_host_capture` / `close_run`, the
+shared host adapter calls `admit_provider_attribution_return(envelope|null,
+planId, producerClosure, stageOrdinal, facts, inventories, enumerationPlan,
+closures, origin)`. Origin is `provider-return` when the wrapper produced the
+envelope and `host-internal` if the host constructed records itself.
+
+**Producer mapping** (one shared law; portable occupancy identity stays distinct
+from opaque payload identity):
+
+| Mode | Worker | Wrapper supply |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ts-tsconfig`, `js-allowjs`, `js-synthesized` | typescript-semantic major 2, unchanged frames | After fact2 mint, emit one V2 per minted `imports@resolved-target` / `references@resolved-binding` / `calls@resolved-callee` / `control-flow@syntactic` / `reachability@from-resolved-calls` fact the compiler-native table can attribute, or omit that fact (unknown). File first-party: `evaluationNativeId` = inventory LogicalPath. Package first-party: `evaluationNativeId` = packageName and `packageManifestPath` = row.path. External file/package as V2 occupancy=external. Symbols MAY omit (exact-id ephemeral) or identity-map. Syntactic import/reference/call rungs MUST omit. |
+| `rust-cargo`, `rust-cargo-prepared` | rust-semantic protocol major 3, unchanged frames | Same envelope and occupancy law. rustc/cargo resolved path vs package fills the wrapper table during the same encoding that writes SubjectIdV1. |
+| `syntax-only` | syntax universe | Omit the envelope, or omit every file/package occupancy record. MUST NOT invent file/package occupancy from specifier text. |
+| clone/candidate | candidate algorithms | Omit. Member IDs are never evaluation-subject identity. |
+
+**Missing envelope** is lawful occupancy-unknown except exact-id ephemeral; it is
+not `required-output-pointer-omitted`. Present partial records are lawful
+omission of unlisted facts. Extra records whose `sourceFactId` is not a minted
+fact of this producer/stage refuse. Records are strict unique utf-8 of
+`sourceFactId`. A refused envelope captures nothing.
+
+**C15.** If ephemeral exact-id first-party identity `I_eph` disagrees with sidecar
+first-party identity `I_sc`, refuse `TARGET_ATTRIBUTION_EPHEMERAL_IDENTITY_CONFLICT`.
+Independently known identity is not overwritten.
+
+**Public route.** Internal keys stay internal. Existing evaluator-fault pairs:
+`input-schema-invalid:provider-return` and `input-join-invalid:provider-return`
+→ `EVALUATION.INPUT_REFUSED` / `PROVIDER.PROTOCOL_VIOLATION`; host-invented
+mapping uses origin `host-internal` → `HOST.INVARIANT_VIOLATED`. No new
+DomainDetailCode, no new D9 code. LIVE D9 successor-artifact is not discharged.
+
+Host MUST NOT parse `SubjectIdV1` namespace:opaque spelling and MUST NOT treat
+arbitrary host filesystem or package-manager data as provider attestation.
